Academic position in Speech Pathology (B, C or D) •\tGuide, inspire, and grow the next generation of leaders in speech pathology.\n•\tUC Level B, C or D, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $187,557 pa plus 17% Super\n•\tFull Time, Continuing Opportunity Job no: 504682 Work type: Academic Location: Bruce Categories: Speech Pathology Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Guide, inspire, and grow the next generation of leaders in speech pathology. UC Level B, C or D, Salary Range $116,403 pa - $187,557 pa plus 17% Super Full Time, Continuing Opportunity About us: At the University of Canberra, we’re a welcoming and connected academic community shaped by the people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. Our research focuses on real-world challenges, working alongside partners to create outcomes that matter, while our teaching builds confidence and capability for the future. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, UC is a place where you can grow ideas, contribute knowledge, and make a difference. About the role: The Faculty of Health is seeking an experienced academic to join our Discipline of Speech Pathology as a either Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer or Associate Professor (ER/EF) pending experience level. This is an exciting opportunity to play a pivotal role in advancing the discipline’s teaching, research, and professional engagement. In this role, you will contribute to curriculum renewal and development, collaborate with the team to design innovative approaches to teaching delivery, and provide high-quality teaching within our Masters program. You will will also lead impactful research that strengthens the profession and community outcomes. The position provides the opportunity to foster strong relationships with industry partners, professional associations, and key stakeholders locally, nationally, and internationally to enhance the disciplines objectives. For senior candidates, you will have the opportunity to take on  leadership roles to provide strategic leadership within the speech pathology team and broader Faculty. Key responsibilities include: Supporting students in both classroom and clinical environments Collaborating with colleagues to advance academic initiatives and research Delivering innovative, high-quality teaching in the Masters program and contribute to curriculum design. Developing and maintaining strong partnerships with industry, professional associations, and government stakeholders. Promoting a culture of collaboration, innovation, and excellence Providing strategic leadership for the Discipline of Speech Pathology in education and research (for Level C & D). Mentoring and supporting academic staff to enhance teaching quality and research outcomes (for Level C & D). About you: You’re a dedicated educator and researcher ready to shape the future of speech pathology. You bring expertise in one or more of the focus areas listed above and a commitment to inclusive, evidence-based practice. The successful applicant will have strong interpersonal skills and the ability to communicate and establish effective relationships with staff, students and industry stakeholders. For Level C & D, a track record of internationally recognised research publications, higher degree research student supervision and success in securing grant funding will also be required. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid Australian working rights at the time of submission. A current ACT working with vulnerable people (WWVP) registration. Or able to obtain A PhD in Speech Pathology or a closely related field. Eligible for (or currently hold) Certified Practising Speech Pathologist status with Speech Pathology Australia. How to apply: Please apply with you CV and a cover letter (1-2 pages) outlining your interest and suitability for the level for which you wish to be considered. Please ensure you align your CV with the position description requirements as linked below Position Description - Lecturer in Speech Pathology (Level B) Position Description - Senior Lecturer in Speech Pathology (Level C) Position Description - Associate Professor in Speech Pathology (Level D) For job specific information: please contact Claire Pearce - Discipline Lead Speech Pathology andOccupational Therapy - Claire.Pearce@canberra.edu.au - +61 2 6206 8452. For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UC Talent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 20 September 2026 Advertised: 28 Aug 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Sear