Senior Advisor, Research Tenders •\tShape impactful research partnerships and drive tender success\n•\tUC Level 7, Salary Range $103,259 pa - $111,865 pa plus 17% Super\n•\tFull Time, Continuing Opportunity Job no: 504687 Work type: Professional Location: Bruce Categories: Research Support Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results View position description Shape impactful research partnerships and drive tender success UC Level 7, Salary Range $103,259 pa - $111,865 pa plus 17% Super Full Time, Continuing Opportunity About us: At the University of Canberra, we’re a welcoming and connected academic community shaped by the people, cultures and environments of Australia’s capital. Our research focuses on real-world challenges, working alongside partners to create outcomes that matter, while our teaching builds confidence and capability for the future. Ranked number one in Canberra for graduate employment, skills development and student support, UC is a place where you can grow ideas, contribute knowledge, and make a difference. About the role: UC is recruiting for a motivated and detail-oriented Senior Advisor, Research Tenders to join our Research Grants team. This exciting opportunity for an experienced grants, contracts, tendering, or research management professional to play an important role in securing strategic research partnerships and supporting the University's research excellence. Key responsibilities include: Coordinate the development of high-quality tender submissions. Manage research contracts and agreements and provide expert advice on research opportunities Contribute to increasing research impact and ensure compliance across a diverse portfolio. Collaborate within the Research Grants and Tenders team to deliver high-quality services. Stakeholder management for identifying and managing externally funded tenders matters, in collaboration with and as primary liaison to faculties. Contributing to the policy and procedure in relation to innovation and commercialization, working closely with UC’s Innovation Committee. Maintain tender and contract management systems. About you: If you are an experienced collaborative contracts, tenders, or research management professional looking to make a meaningful contribution to a growing research environment, we’d would love to hear from you. Other skills and attributes required for this role are: Demonstrated experience in tender and contract management, grant administration, research administration, or a related field. Strong writing and editing skills, with the ability to prepare persuasive, high-quality tender and proposal submissions. Experience reviewing, negotiating, and administering contracts and agreements. Experience and/or interest in innovation and commercialisation. A high level of attention to detail and commitment to quality and compliance. Excellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills. Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines simultaneously. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and project coordination capabilities. Experience working within the higher education, government, research, or consultancy sectors will be highly regarded. Offerings/ Benefits/ Culture: The University offers excellent conditions and benefits which can be further explored on our “ Work at UC ” site such as flexible, family-friendly policies, on site gym, on site medical services, a grocery store, and Early Childhood Education and Care facilities. We believe people deserve to feel welcome, supported, and empowered to realise their potential. Being a values based organisation, UC sets a goal to be the national sector leader in equity, diversity, inclusion and access via our Reconnected Strategy . UC encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people with disability, neurodiversity and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Eligibility: Applicants who wish to apply for this position should have valid working rights at the time of submission. How to apply: Please apply with you Resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and suitability. Also, please ensure you take the time to align your Resume with the Position Description requirements. We want to understand how your skills and experience relate to this position. If you are initially shortlisted, you may be asked to complete a written assessment. For job specific information: please contact Helene Rushby - Manager, Research Grants - Helene.Rushby@canberra.edu.au - 02 6201 2181. For recruitment and application questions: please contact the Talent Solutions team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au . We recognise people communicate and process information differently, and we support multiple ways to participate in the recruitment evaluation. For reasonable adjustment, please reach out to the UCTalent team. Closing date: 11.55pm, Sunday 20 September 2026 Advertised: 28 Aug 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Senior Advisor, Research Tenders Bruce 20 Sep 2026 •\tShape impactful research partnerships and drive tender success\n•\tUC Level 7, Salary Range $103,259 pa - $111,865 pa plus 17% Super\n•\tFull Time, Continuing Opportunity Featured jobs No features opportunities currently available Current jobs Position Location Closes Senior Advisor, Research Tenders Bruce 20 Sep 2026 •\tShape impactful research partnerships and drive tender success\n•\tUC Level 7, Salary Range $103,259 pa - $111,865 pa plus 17% Super\n•\tFull Time, Continuing Opportunity Expressions