Ngunnawal Centre Study Coach - Talent Pool Upload your CV to register for casual Ngunnawal Centre Study Coach positions Job no: 501436 Work type: Casual Professional Location: Bruce Categories: Administration, Student Support Apply for this job Refer a friend Back to search results Do you wish to be contacted when a position becomes available for a Ngunnawal Centre Study Coach? The Ngunnawal Centre is our University of Canberra Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander student success and support centre. Our friendly staff are committed to better university access, participation, and opportunities for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. Operating under general direction and reporting to the Ngunnawal Centre Manager, Ngunnawal Centre Study Coaches will use specialist knowledge in their discipline area to provide knowledge and culturally safe academic support and skills development for Indigenous students. Ngunnawal Centre Study Coaches have a critical role in supporting students to successfully continue in their course, with a goal of achieving improved learning outcomes, successful course progression and ultimately course completion. Some of the responsibilities of a Ngunnawal Centre Study Coach are to engage 1:1 with Indigenous students to develop tutoring plans, use learning, and support tools available to students within the university to increase their learning capacity and engagement with their studies. As a Ngunnawal Centre Study Coach you will be committed to empowering our students academically, professionally, and personally. To be considered for upcoming positions you will require a WWVP, demonstrated discipline expertise and an understanding of how relevant subjects are taught at UC. As this is a position in support of our Aboriginal and/ Torres Strait Islander students, it is important to have an awareness and respect of cultural sensitivities to ensure the best support for the student’s success. Study Coaches will be required to meet the following criteria: Must be UC Honours, Postgraduate, or HDR students Must attend mandatory paid training delivered by Study Skills. This training covers coaching strategies to support academic integrity and promote an empowering, student‑led learning approach. Must complete: A student–coach work plan at the start of each semester, and End‑of‑semester reporting for each student they support. To register your interest to become a Study Coach for the Ngunnawal Centre, please complete the online application form highlighting your discipline specialisation along with your CV and submit it to ensure your application is complete. If your personal details or your situation changes, please note you will be able to update your application as needed. Advertised: 06 Aug 2024 AUS Eastern Standard Time Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Ngunnawal Centre Study Coach - Talent Pool Bruce 31 Jan 2027 Upload your CV to register for casual Ngunnawal Centre Study Coach positions Featured jobs No features opportunities currently available Current jobs Position Location Closes Ngunnawal Centre Study Coach - Talent Pool Bruce 31 Jan 2027 Upload your CV to register for casual Ngunnawal Centre Study Coach positions Expressions of interest Upload your CV to register for positions Professional Talent Pool register (Casual and Fixed Term) Ngunnawal Centre Study Coach - Talent Pool Casual Academic Staff Talent Pool - Faculty of Business Government & Law Casual Academic Staff Talent Pool - Faculty of Arts and Design Casual Academic Staff Talent Pool - Faculty of Education Casual Academic Staff Talent Pool - Faculty of Health Casual Academic Staff Talent Pool -  Faculty of Science and Technology Powered by PageUp Back to Work at UC Subscribe to job alerts Stay updated on job openings that meet your skills and interests. Subscribe to job alerts Search for a job Work type Casual Professional (1) Location Bruce (1) Category Administration (1) Student Support (1) Back to Work at UC Navigate back to the main page of our careers section. Go to Work at UC Job application guide Learn how to apply for jobs at UC with our guide. View frequently asked questions and learn helpful tips on preparing your application and interviewing. Learn how to apply Other quick links Contact us Future students Current students Alumni contact us Donors General enquiries Faculties Arts and Design Business, Government and Law Education Health Science and Technology News and events UnCover Newsroom Find an expert Events Blog Services Security Library Medical and Counselling IT Service updates Gym Accommodation Administration Maps Job opportunities Staff directory Researcher profiles Freedom of information Policies and procedures University of Canberra, Bruce ACT 2617 Australia +61 2 6201 5111 ABN 81 633 873 422 CRICOS 00212K TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12003 (Australian University) Contact UC Copyright Disclaimer Privacy Accessibility Collection notice UC acknowledges the Ngunnawal people, traditional custodians of the lands where Bruce campus is situated. We wish to acknowledge and respect their continuing culture and the contribution they make to the life of Canberra and the region. We also acknowledge all other First Nations Peoples on whose lands we gather."
