Maps Safety & Support UC Open Day Fest - For future students, families, and the whole community. Saturday 12 September, 10am to 3pm UC Open Day Fest - Saturday 12 September, 10am to 3pm UC Open Day Fest Sat 12 Sept, 10am–3pm REGISTER NOW Work at UC Browse jobs Home / About UC / Work at UC Why work at UC? At the University of Canberra, we dare to be curious. Globally recognised for reducing inequalities, we are a community that celebrates differences, embraces similarities and values unique contributions. With over 100,000 alumni from more than 100 countries, we hold a strong reputation for producing profession-ready graduates and problem-solving research. We believe inclusion inspires innovation and equity, where diversity and access are at the heart of everything we do. As a UC staff member, you’ll have the opportunity to channel your skills towards a greater purpose. Whether this be through teaching, research, support, advice, in a hybrid arrangement, or on campus, you’ll play a vital role in our ongoing success. Browse our job list Currently a UC staff member? View our internal job opportunies for a career change. Flexibility and leave benefits Flexibility and leave benefits Hybrid working arrangements We highly value workplace flexibility to enhance our employees' work-life balance. Depending on the nature of the role, staff can access hybrid working arrangements to provide work-life balance and flexibility, and accommodate the needs of our diverse workforce. Many of our staff have a hybrid working arrangement with 3 days on campus and 2 days working at home. Generous leave benefits We also offer generous and supportive workplace conditions with many different leave benefits. Our staff enjoy four weeks of recreational leave and 20 days of personal/carers leave annually, plus additional time off during our end-of-year shutdown period. Learn more Financial and corporate benefits Financial and corporate benefits UC offers nationally competitive remuneration with annual salary increments, as well as 17% employer superannuation contributions. Additionally, our staff can take advantage of numerous salary packaging options, including superannuation, childcare services and on campus parking. We also offer the option to salary package vehicles via novated lease or self-managed leases, in addition to other eligible benefits. Learn more Training and career development Training and career development We are passionate about your ongoing professional development as a UC staff member. Further your career through your own professional development plan, take advantage of our professional development weeks, online training, our outside studies program, mentoring, study assistance and more. At UC, we both encourage and support staff to pursue internal job opportunities. We have an Internal Talent Program, designed to assist staff with upskilling and career development, as well as coaching in CV development, interview skills, networking and more. Learn more Workplace culture and wellbeing Workplace culture and wellbeing Our people are at the centre of everything we do. We value the uniqueness of everyone and the diverse range of perspectives, experiences, and ideas that our employees bring to UC. For our people to reach their full potential, we are committed to providing an environment where everyone feels they belong and can bring their whole selves to work. Accreditations and memberships UC has sought and gained a number of accreditations and affiliations to help us in supporting our people to feel included, valued and respected so they are able to fully participate at work. We are proud to have the following accreditations and affiliations. Diversity Council of Australia Member Pride in Diversity Member Australian Disability Network Member Breastfeeding Friendly Workplace Athena Swan Bronze Award Learn more Values and purpose Our purpose statement and values define us, guiding the University of Canberra's pursuit of academic excellence through quality education, student success and impactful research. The refresh, led by over 250 staff contributions, underscores our positive culture. We are committed to fostering and integrating values-driven initiatives at UC. Read about our values and purpose Academic excellence We have a vibrant and respected research community that has established UC as a research-led institution, committed to global change. We want to build the best environment for us to excel in this core endeavour, and in so doing, ensure we are fully connected to our students, our staff and our place. Learn about UC's academic excellence My passion for education and making a difference in students’ learning experience drives me every day to try innovative ways of teaching. My friendly and collaborative colleagues make the workplace wonderful. Dr Richa Awasthy Assistant Professor Faculty of Science & Technology My passion for education and making a difference in students’ learning experience drives me every day to try innovative ways of teaching. My friendly and collaborative colleagues make the workplace wonderful. Dr Richa Awasthy Assistant Professor Faculty of Science & Technology I am a proud Canberran and Indigenous academic. I’ve been working at UC since 2019. I love working at UC because of its inclusivity on behalf of its staff and the students. Erina Mikus-Fletcher Lecturer Faculty of Business, Government & Law I am a proud Canberran and Indigenous academic. I’ve been working at UC since 2019. I love working at UC because of its inclusivity on behalf of its staff and the students. Erina Mikus-Fletcher Lecturer Faculty of Business, Government & Law l love the strong focus on equity and accessibility here at UC. Throughout my career, I’ve had to navigate socioeconomic and racial prejudices. Here, I can help motivate students who feel isolation or face inequalities. Layal Naji Lecturer, Vision Science and Optometry Faculty of Health l love the strong focus on equity and accessibility here at UC. Throughout my career, I’ve had to navigate socioeconomic and racial prejudices. Here, I can help motivate students who feel isolation or face inequalities. Layal Naji Lecturer, Vision Science and Optometry Faculty of Health UC positively challenges me. I learn something new every day and I am so lucky to work with an incredible group of people, whom I value immensely. Ethan Althofer Program Manager, People & Diversity UC positively challenges me. I learn something new every day and I am so lucky to work with an incredible group of people, whom I value immensely. Ethan Althofer Program Manager, People & Diversity An exciting opportunity at UC arose that led me to make the move to Canberra. Today, I am still with UC and genuinely enjoy working here. The environment is positive and nurturing. Kyle Luo Advisor Research Grants An exciting opportunity at UC arose that led me to make the move to Canberra. Today, I am still with UC and genuinely enjoy working here. The environment is positive and nurturing. Kyle Luo Advisor Research Grants I thought I’d be in Canberra 3 years… 14 years later, I wouldn't change it for the world. I love working at UC – not only do I feel I’m a valued member of my team, but also in UC’s broader community. Kirsten Povey Executive Advisor Finance I thought I’d be in Canberra 3 years… 14 years later, I wouldn't change it for the world. I love working at UC – not only do I feel I’m a valued member of my team, but also in UC’s broader community. Kirsten Povey Executive Advisor Finance My passion for education and making a difference in students’ learning experience drives me every day to try innovative ways of teaching. My friendly and collaborative colleagues make the workplace wonderful. Dr Richa Awasthy Assistant Professor Faculty of Science & Technology My passion for education and making a difference in students’ learning experience drives me every day to try innovative ways of teaching. My friendly and collaborative colleagues make 