. Layal Naji Lecturer, Vision Science and Optometry Faculty of Health UC positively challenges me. I learn something new every day and I am so lucky to work with an incredible group of people, whom I value immensely. Ethan Althofer Program Manager, People & Diversity UC positively challenges me. I learn something new every day and I am so lucky to work with an incredible group of people, whom I value immensely. Ethan Althofer Program Manager, People & Diversity 1 of 6 2 of 6 3 of 6 4 of 6 5 of 6 6 of 6 Living in Canberra Surrounded by iconic Australian bushland with a bustling city centre, Canberra has all the benefits of both big city and small-town living. Canberra is rich in opportunity. Not only is the city famous for museums and galleries, world-class dining and entertainment, Canberra is known for its inclusive community and diversity, with a quarter of the city’s population born overseas. Everyone is welcome, and everyone is encouraged to succeed. Learn more about living in Canberra Relocation support If you need to relocate to join UC, we may offer relocation as part of your employment offer pending your position. Most Academic appointments with a minimum of 3 years duration are eligible to receive a relocation allowance to contribute towards your move to Canberra. Upon successful application to UC, your offer of employment will outline your specific entitlements. You will also have an Employee Experience Coordinator (EECO) to provide you with guidance and support around UC’s relocation process once you accept your offer. You may also be interested in... Our 10-year strategy Indigenous Leadership Strategy Our faculties and schools Campus facilities Talk to us If you have questions about a specific job advertised, please get in touch with the contact person listed on the advertisement. For all other enquiries related to your career with us, please get in touch with our UC Talent team on 02 6206 3867 or email uctalent@canberra.edu.au Email us Other quick links Also of interest Information for Employers Career connections Jobs at UC Contact us Future students Current students Alumni contact us Donors General enquiries Faculties Arts and Design Business, Government and Law Education Health Science and Technology News and events UnCover Newsroom Find an expert Events Blog Services Security Library Medical and Counselling IT Service updates Gym Accommodation Administration Maps Job opportunities Staff directory Researcher profiles Freedom of information Policies and procedures University of Canberra, Bruce ACT 2617 Australia +61 2 6201 5111 ABN 81 633 873 422 CRICOS 00212K TEQSA Provider ID: PRV12003 (Australian University) Contact UC Copyright Disclaimer Privacy Accessibility Collection notice UC acknowledges the Ngunnawal people, traditional custodians of the lands where Bruce campus is situated. We wish to acknowledge and respect their continuing culture and the contribution they make to the life of Canberra and the region. We also acknowledge all other First Nations Peoples on whose lands we gather."
